<name>Heater &amp; Air Conditioner System</name>
<para id="RM0000005L5013X" category="C" type-id="300BD" name-id="5228I-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B1423/23</dtccode>
<dtcname>Refrigerant pressure malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005L5013X_05" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AJT00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>This code is output when the refrigerant pressure is abnormally low (0.176MPa{1.8kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>} or less) or abnormally high (3.025MPa{30.9kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>} or more).</ptxt>
<ptxt>The air conditioner tube &amp; accessory assembly (pressure sensor) is installed on the high-pressure side piping to detect refrigerant pressure, and outputs the refrigerant pressure as a signal to the air conditioner amplifier assembly. The air conditioner amplifier assembly converts the signal into pressure data according to the sensor characteristics and controls the compressor.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="0.99in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.27in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.82in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Diagnosis Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Abnormal Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Malfunction Duration</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B1423/23</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Refrigerant pressure signal malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Current malfunction only</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Air conditioner tube &amp; accessory assembly (pressure sensor)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire harness and connector (air conditioner amplifier assembly - air conditioner tube &amp; accessory assembly (pressure sensor))</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Air Conditioner Amplifier Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Cooler piping (leak, clog)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Cooler expansion valve (clog, stuck)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Condenser assembly (reduced cooling capacity due to clog or dirt)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Cooler dryer (unable to absorb moisture in refrigerant cycle)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Cooling fan system (unable to cool condenser)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
