<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the pressure sensor connector.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the connectors connected, remove the air conditioner amplifier assembly from the vehicle.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between the terminals of the connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E132747J31" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.65in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A9 (PRE) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON(A/C OFF)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.7V to 4.8V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the measured voltage is not within the normal range, the air conditioner amplifier assembly, pressure sensor or wire harness may be malfunctioning, or the refrigerant amount may be incorrect.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005L5013X_08_0014" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000005L5013X_08_0020" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000005L5013X_08_0014" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AJZ00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Air Conditioner Tube &amp; Accessory Assembly (Pressure Sensor Output Circuit)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between the air conditioner amplifier assembly connector terminals when the following conditions are met.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E132747J31" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If the pressure on the high-pressure piping side becomes too high during inspection (voltage exceeds 4.8V), the fail-safe operates and the compressor stops compression. Therefore, measure the voltage until the fail-safe operates.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The problem symptom may recur after some time, so it is necessary to check for a certain period (approximately 10 minutes).</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>When the outside air temperature is low (-1.5°C or less), the compressor is stopped by normal operation of the evaporator temperature sensor to prevent the evaporator from freezing. In that case, perform this inspection indoors in a warm place.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
