<testgrp id="RM0000005L5013X_08_0029" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AK900000">
<testtitle>Charge Refrigerant HFC-134a (R134a)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>If refrigerant is charged without sufficient evacuation, moisture in the air remaining in the cooling system may freeze in the expansion valve and clog the high-pressure piping side. Therefore, recover the refrigerant once, perform sufficient evacuation to remove moisture from the system, charge the correct amount of refrigerant, and check whether the diagnostic trouble code is output.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Recover the refrigerant using a refrigerant recovery unit.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform evacuation.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Charge the correct amount of refrigerant. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000N8300CX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005L5013X_08_0030" fin="false">NEXT</down>
