<test1>
<ptxt>Check the diagnostic trouble codes under the following conditions.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>A diagnostic trouble code is output when the pressure on the high-pressure piping side becomes high. Therefore, the diagnostic trouble code may be output after some time, so it is necessary to check after a certain period (approximately 10 minutes) has elapsed.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When the outside air temperature is low (-1.5°C or less), the compressor is stopped by normal operation of the evaporator temperature sensor to prevent the evaporator from freezing. In that case, perform this inspection indoors in a warm place.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If refrigerant is charged without sufficient evacuation, moisture in the air remaining in the system may freeze in the expansion valve and clog the high-pressure side piping. Therefore, recover the refrigerant once, perform sufficient evacuation, then charge the correct amount of refrigerant and check whether the diagnostic trouble code is output. However, if the diagnostic trouble code is no longer output after this work, it indicates that the dryer in the condenser is unable to absorb moisture in the refrigerant cycle, so the dryer must be replaced.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
